WEBVTT

NOTE Internet Monitor tour: speed (en). Generated by tools/tutorial/build.cjs.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:05.900
The Speed test page measures how fast your
internet really is, using Cloudflare's servers.

2
00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:07.433
Press Start test.

3
00:00:07.433 --> 00:00:10.567
A test takes about a
minute and uses some data,

4
00:00:10.567 --> 00:00:13.767
so on a small data plan,
don't run it too often.

5
00:00:14.167 --> 00:00:17.709
First the app measures latency,
then download, then upload.

6
00:00:17.709 --> 00:00:20.951
The gauge shows the live
speed in megabits per second,

7
00:00:20.951 --> 00:00:23.833
and the box that is lit
is the step running now.

8
00:00:24.233 --> 00:00:27.381
When it finishes, the gauge
shows your download speed.

9
00:00:27.381 --> 00:00:30.353
If it is below the alert
level you set in Settings,

10
00:00:30.353 --> 00:00:33.967
a warning says so, and the app
can tell you on your phone too.

11
00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:38.356
These three boxes hold the results:
latency, download and upload.

12
00:00:38.356 --> 00:00:42.100
Compare download and upload with
the speeds in your contract.

13
00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:45.404
Lag under load is graded from A plus to F.

14
00:00:45.404 --> 00:00:50.658
It shows how much slower replies get
while the line is busy. A or B is good.

15
00:00:50.658 --> 00:00:55.567
C or worse means calls and games lag
when someone downloads or uploads.

16
00:00:55.967 --> 00:01:01.151
The numbers show the delay when idle,
while downloading, and while uploading.

17
00:01:01.151 --> 00:01:05.999
With a poor grade, turning on SQM or
QoS in the router usually fixes it.

18
00:01:05.999 --> 00:01:09.500
If the router has no such option,
ask your provider.

19
00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:13.563
Today's tests lists every test
from today with its lag grade,

20
00:01:13.563 --> 00:01:17.167
and whether you started it
yourself or it ran on a schedule.

21
00:01:17.567 --> 00:01:20.757
To test automatically,
for example every two hours,

22
00:01:20.757 --> 00:01:23.258
set Run automatically every in Settings.

23
00:01:23.258 --> 00:01:28.700
Tests at different times of day show when
your line slows down, such as in the evening.

24
00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:30.290
Every test is saved.

25
00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:33.325
The monthly report compares
them with the speed you

26
00:01:33.325 --> 00:01:36.300
pay for, which is strong
evidence for a complaint.

27
00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:41.767
Press How this page works on any page to
watch its video. Thanks for watching!
